# Bad DNS error (15/09/2026)

PC:DESKTOP-UT50TBB
Path: Ethernet -> TL-SG108S -> BT Hub (192.168.1.254)
Fault: DNS set to this PC (127.0.0.1 and ::1)  
Symptom: Internet by number works, names do not.
Ladder
- Physical — Cable into TL-SG108S. First Ethernet was 169.254.x.x (no DHCP). After link up: 192.168.1.103.
- Local IP — ipconfig /all. 192.168.1.103/24, DHCP yes, suffix home.
- Gateway — 192.168.1.254. ping 1.1.1.1 about 20ms.
- DNS — Wi-Fi off. DNS ::1 and 127.0.0.1. nslookup: no response from ::1. ping 1.1.1.1 still OK. After ipconfig /flushdns, ping google.com: could not find host.
- Routing — Skipped. WAN already proven by 1.1.1.1.
- Firewall — Not this fault.
- App — Names failed, not the browser.
Cause: DNS pointed at localhost. Cache hid it until flush. Wi-Fi and IPv6 DNS also hid it until they were off.
Fix: Ethernet DNS back to Automatic.
Proof: nslookup google.com via bthub.home. ping google.com replies.
Next time: Wi-Fi off, break IPv4 and IPv6 DNS, flush cache before saying it still works.
